	<div class="row bg-light p-6 rounded-5 mb-18">
		<div class="column p-6 rounded-5 bg-light mb-18">
			<div class="pvlRichtext"><h3 data-pm-slice="1 1 []"><strong>Make Christmas Brighter for a Child</strong></h3>
<p><span>Adopt an Angel through The Salvation Army of the Midlands and help provide Christmas gifts for local children, from newborn through age 12, whose families are facing financial hardship.</span></p>
<p><strong>How to Participate</strong></p>
<ol data-spread="false">
<li>
<p><span>Click “Adopt an Angel” to select your Angels.</span></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><span>Shop using each child’s wish list and clothing sizes.</span></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><span>Keep gifts in their original packaging and leave them unwrapped.</span></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><span>Label each child’s gifts with their Angel Number.</span></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><span>Return gifts by December 11, 2026.</span><span></span></p>
</li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Adopting as a Group?</strong></p>
<p><span>Businesses, churches, schools, and community groups can adopt multiple Angels and work together to fulfill their wish lists. For group adoptions or printed Angel tags, contact Shannon Chapman at </span><a href="mailto:Shannon.Chapman@uss.salvationarmy.org"><span>Shannon.Chapman@uss.salvationarmy.org</span></a><span> or 803-309-3244.</span></p>
<p><span></span></p>
<p><strong>Gift Drop-Off Dates and Locations</strong></p>
<p><strong>November 30–December 4</strong><br><span>Monday–Friday, 9:00 a.m.–3:00 p.m.</span><br><span>The Salvation Army</span><br><span>3024 Farrow Road, Columbia, SC 29203</span></p>
<p><strong>December 5</strong><br><span>Saturday, 8:30 a.m.–11:30 a.m.</span></p>
<p><strong>December 7–11</strong><br><span>Monday–Friday, 9:00 a.m.–4:00 p.m.</span></p>
<p><strong>Both December drop-off periods take place at:</strong><br><span>The Christmas Warehouse</span><br><span>South Carolina State Fairgrounds, George Nutt Cattle Arena</span><br><span>1200 Rosewood Drive, Columbia, SC 29201</span></p>
<p><em><strong>Thank you for helping bring Christmas joy to children across the Midlands!</strong></em></p></div>
		</div>
	</div>
